@fxn which character encoding do you expect `request.params` to use when you instantiate a `ActionDispatch::Request`?

If the controller is not know, the character encoding should be binary and I think the encoding validation would pass for any input.

I think that is a better change than making the parameters UTF-8 and not validating the input.

@rafaelfranca That's a great question.

I also believe it should be binary, meaning, we don't know at this point.

Because `AD::Request` is not a generic class that you can instantiate anywhere (for which [default encodings](https://github.com/rails/rails/blob/5adb6a9a98a33c699b184fdb6f38ddea740fbe86/railties/lib/rails.rb#L20-L24) would probably be the natural choice), but a class intended to help in middleware, and that models the request object in controllers. In this constrained context, I think the natural encoding is binary, and we can document that.
